{"seq":17,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:57:25.587Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7bcfd73a56cf26332e01efccb372b710192033cd5dafbcafa091f739c9ea24c9","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files (4 North digests, 2 Central). Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n2. *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. The same note has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\nWorth knowing before this goes in the deck:\n• Marcus's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's) also lists *#4419* for QFL, but describes it as Gate 3 printer lag on BOL printouts, not the scanner problem. One of the two descriptions is probably wrong, so check the real ticket before you put it on a slide.\n• Moss's other QFL notes (9/14/2025 pipeline digest, 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't have any ticket numbers.\n• The Central notes have #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are all Marrow, not QFL.\n• Moss's cheat sheet also warns not to mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways, a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:57:31.717Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"4149ecfacf85f4f718bd7aaabc23f28fb25da9e3aef18ce1c28e519e8b95f788","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I've sent you the list in our DM. I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared team files, and only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n1. **#4419**, from Moss's undated North cheat sheet (`teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md`). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. **#PD-4492**, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note dated 5 Oct 2025 (`teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md`). Thea opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix the next day.\n\nBefore this goes in the deck:\n- **#4419 has two different descriptions.** Marcus's own note from 14 Jul 2025 (not one of Moss's) gives the same number but calls it Gate 3 printer lag on bill-of-lading printouts. One of the two is probably wrong, so check the actual ticket before you put it on a slide.\n- **Moss's other two QFL notes have no ticket numbers.** Those are the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in.\n- **Moss's Central notes aren't about QFL.** They mention #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for Marrow accounts.\n- **Don't mix up the names.** Quarendon Freightways is a different company and isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
